<title>USA: District of Columbia deal yields 5.92 pct in 2017.</title>
<headline>District of Columbia deal yields 5.92 pct in 2017.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Wednesday it tentatively priced $50 million District of Columbia refunding bonds at a top yield of 5.92 percent in 2017.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>DISTRICT OF COLUMBIA</p>
<p>RE: $50,000,000*</p>
<p>Revenue Refunding Bonds</p>
<p>(The Howard University Issue)</p>
<p>Series 1996</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>		 A Confirmed</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 09/15/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 04/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 10/01</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>10/01/1997		  335M    4.00  %	100.00</p>
<p>10/01/1998		  280M    4.30  %	  4.35</p>
